WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.201
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.603
We are hanging out with
the one and only Kristen Bell!

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:07.006
And we are about to play
a brand-new game

00:00:07.006 --> 00:00:10.743
called "You Can Only Keep One."

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:12.479
-♪ You can only keep,
you can keep ♪

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:14.681
♪ You can only keep one ♪

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.749
-This is based on
the popular Internet trend.

00:00:16.749 --> 00:00:18.951
Each round, I'm going to
give you three choices,

00:00:18.951 --> 00:00:21.054
and you'll have to tell me
which of the three

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:24.123
you would keep
if you could only keep one.

00:00:24.123 --> 00:00:26.159
-Okay.
-All right?

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:28.427 line:0%
Let's see the first
three options. All right.

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:31.631 line:0%
We have French fries,
curly fries, or waffle fries.

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.933 line:0%
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:38.270 line:0%
-How is anyone supposed to
make this decision?

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:39.939 line:0%
-Well -- I know.
All right. Wait. Let's --

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.641 line:0%
I've got an answer, I think.
You can only keep one.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.476 line:0%
-Okay, I think I do, too.
Let's see if we agree.

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:45.245 line:0%
Let's say it at the same time.

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:46.446 line:0%
-Hmm.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:48.881 line:0%
-Both: One, two, three.

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:50.382 line:0%
-French fries.
-Curly fries.

00:00:50.382 --> 00:00:53.586 line:0%
-Wow! Wow!

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.120 line:0%
-Why'd you pick French fries?

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.558 line:0%
The most boring
of all the fries.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.626 line:0%
-It's also -- It's just classic.

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:01.894 line:0%
-Okay.
-I went classic.

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:03.796 line:0%
I just don't want
to see them go away.

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:06.032 line:0%
And so I was just thinking
about the future and --

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.433 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:11.070 line:0%
-Oh, God. Wait. If we choose,
the rest of them go away?!

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.972 line:0%
-No, no, no.
That's not part of the game.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.974 line:0%
No, they don't go away.
I was just thinking --

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:17.009 line:0%
Well, you're the one
playing the game, not me.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:18.978 line:0%
All right. Next round.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.813 line:0%
Your options are --
This is a toughie.

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:23.950 line:0%
"The Little Mermaid,"
"Aladdin," "Lion King."

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.052 line:0%
-I gotta go.
-No, no, no. You can't go!

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:27.486 line:0%
-I have to go.

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:29.322 line:0%
I just found out
I'm not available right now.

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:30.490 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.757 line:0%
-Kristen!
-I'm so sorry.

00:01:31.757 --> 00:01:33.192 line:0%
-Look at this.

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:36.195 line:0%
"Little Mermaid," "Aladdin,"
"Lion King."

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:40.433 line:0%
Your kids are in that age.
I mean, these are classics.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:42.569 line:0%
-Jimmy.

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:46.306 line:0%
Can I get fired from Disney
if I tell you my real answer?

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:48.041 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.342 line:0%
Do we think?

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:51.010 line:0%
Like, can we have the lawyers
check into it?

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.945 line:0%
Okay, okay. I'm going to go
with my gut instinct

00:01:52.945 --> 00:01:55.048 line:0%
'cause it was my favorite.

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:56.983 line:0%
I got --
I think I got to keep "Aladdin."

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:59.752 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.453 line:0%
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:01.453 --> 00:02:02.856 line:0%
-"Aladdin."
-I really --

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:06.325 line:0%
I like his scrappiness.
I loved Abu.

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:09.828 line:0%
-I like the live version.

00:02:09.828 --> 00:02:11.597 line:0%
I saw the Broadway version.
That's good.

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:14.367 line:0%
But you've got to go
"Little Mermaid," right?

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.568 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:16.769 line:0%
"Lion King"?

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.170 line:0%
[ Louder cheers and applause ]

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:19.738 line:0%
"Lion King"
is the crowd favorite.

00:02:19.738 --> 00:02:21.340 line:0%
-Yeah, everybody loves
"Lion King."

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.075 line:0%
It's not that I don't like
"Lion King."

00:02:23.075 --> 00:02:24.777 line:0%
-Yeah, me too.
-I do like "Lion King."

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.812 line:0%
I don't know why -- This is,
like, the har-- This is...

00:02:26.812 --> 00:02:28.347 line:0%
-No, this is so fun.
-...too difficult.

00:02:28.347 --> 00:02:29.749 line:0%
-No, this is too fun.

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:31.117 line:0%
All right. Here's the next --
-This is so fun.

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:32.352 line:0%
-Ready for this? How about this?

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:34.187 line:0%
Meryl Streep in
"The Devil Wears Prada."

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:36.188 line:0%
Meryl Streep in "Mamma Mia!"

00:02:36.188 --> 00:02:39.058 line:0%
Or Meryl Streep
in "Little Women."

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:40.592 line:0%
Let's discuss.

00:02:40.592 --> 00:02:42.929 line:0%
[ Audience murmuring ]

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:45.265 line:0%
People are walking out
right now.

00:02:45.265 --> 00:02:47.867 line:0%
They're freaking out.
"I can't take this."

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:49.202 line:0%
-Well, don't -- But listen.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:51.337 line:0%
Everybody who's leaving,
stop for a second.

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.105 line:0%
We're keeping
two out of three Meryls.

00:02:53.105 --> 00:02:54.873 line:0%
-Yes, yes.

00:02:54.873 --> 00:02:56.108 line:0%
-No.
-No.

00:02:56.108 --> 00:02:57.743 line:0%
-We're getting rid
of two out of three Meryls.

00:02:57.743 --> 00:02:59.511 line:0%
I'm not --
-Keeping one Meryl.

00:02:59.511 --> 00:03:02.148 line:0%
-Keeping one Meryl. Okay.
I'm gonna go with this.

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:03.816 line:0%
'Cause it's --
The amount of times

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:06.553 line:0%
I've had to watch "Mamma Mia!"
because my kids love it so much

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:08.554 line:0%
recently.

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:10.022 line:0%
It's got to be "Mamma Mia!"
-The audience likes that.

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:11.991 line:0%
-And she's so cute
in "Mamma Mia!"

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:14.060 line:0%
-Yeah, I'll go with that, too.
I --

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.395 line:0%
"Devil Wears Prada," though.
She really --

00:03:16.395 --> 00:03:18.397 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:18.397 --> 00:03:20.333 line:0%
-Obviously, she killed it
in "The Devil Wears Prada."

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.501 line:0%
-This next one is an insane one.

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.737 line:0%
I think I know the answer
to the next one.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:27.940 line:0%
I'm gonna even write it down.
Do I have paper?

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:29.542 line:0%
I'm gonna write it down.

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:31.477 line:0%
This is kind of an easy one,
I think.

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:33.112 line:0%
-That's a real desk, huh?
It's not a prop desk.

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:35.347 line:0%
There's real paper
in real drawers?

00:03:35.347 --> 00:03:38.184 line:0%
-No, I planned this out.
I planned this bit out earlier.

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:41.287 line:0%
So it's a fake --
-Oh, oh, okay.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:43.089 line:0%
-It's a real --
It's a working desk.

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:45.892 line:0%
I spend all day
working from my desk.

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:47.393 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.761 line:0%
-It's practical. That's what
we say in the movie business.

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:49.929 line:0%
-Yeah. That's so funny.
It actually is a working desk.

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:52.632 line:0%
Yeah. But I don't use it --
Only for talking.

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:54.900 line:0%
Yeah. Not for desking.
All right, ready for this?

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.836 line:0%
This one's gonna
blow your mind.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:58.070 line:0%
-Okay.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:01.507 line:0%
-Red Starburst, pink Starburst,
yellow Starburst.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:05.178 line:0%
-No contest. No contest.
I know my answer.

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:06.678 line:0%
-No contest.

00:04:06.678 --> 00:04:08.013 line:0%
[ Audience shouting ]

00:04:08.013 --> 00:04:10.249 line:0%
-'Cause two of them are gross,
and one of them rules.

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:11.817 line:0%
That's how I know.
-Really?

00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:13.586 line:0%
-Pink.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.755 line:0%
All the way. 100%.

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:17.690 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:20.026 line:0%
This was the easiest one for me.

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:22.695 line:0%
-I went with -- I went with red.

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:25.064 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.866 line:0%
I love red.

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:28.167 line:0%
-See, Jimmy,
if there's one thing

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:31.470 line:0%
that we've learned in life,
it's that we can

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.806 line:0%
still be friends
even if we disagree.

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:35.941 line:0%
-That's right.

00:04:35.941 --> 00:04:38.544 line:0%
That's the one thing
we can actually -- I love that.

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:41.080 line:0%
All right, we can also split
a pack of Starburst

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.248 line:0%
and both be really super happy.

00:04:43.248 --> 00:04:44.917 line:0%
-Exactly!
-All right, bud.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.353 line:0%
Starburst buddies for life.
Kristen Bell, everybody.

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:50.590 line:0%
"Gossip Girl" premieres
July 8th on HBO Max.

